113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (The two motors move with varying speeds mimicking turns. The main idea is to traverse the entire terrain. Think of it like a ripple in water. It starts from the center and moves till it gets to the ends of the body of water. The robot does the same. The varying speeds produce an imbalance in the forces acting on the robot. The robot in turn, swings in that direction with the lower enable values{value given in the program to determine the speed}. As the robot moves in a spiral manner, it ends up moving across the entire terrain )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
